"{\n  \"entities\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Coral Reefs\",\n      \"type\": \"Ecosystem\",\n      \"description\": \"Coral reefs are invaluable underwater ecosystems that play a vital role in supporting marine biodiversity, providing ecosystem services, and contributing to human well-being. They are often referred to as the \\\"rainforests of the sea\\\" due to their incredible biodiversity and importance to marine ecosystems.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Coverage\": \"Less than 1% of the ocean floor\",\n        \"Biodiversity\": \"Home to an estimated 25% of all marine species\",\n        \"Structure\": \"Intricate structures formed by coral polyps secreting calcium carbonate\",\n        \"Importance\": \"Vital to the health of oceans and play a crucial role in supporting both marine and human life\",\n        \"Threats\": \"Climate change, ocean acidification, pollution, overfishing, and destructive fishing practices\",\n        \"Role in Coastal Protection\": \"Act as natural barriers that help to mitigate the destructive effects of natural disasters like hurricanes and tsunamis\",\n        \"Economic Value\": \"Valuable assets for the tourism industry, generating revenue and supporting local economies\",\n        \"Fisheries Support\": \"Support local fisheries by providing a source of income and livelihood for coastal communities that depend on fishing for their sustenance\",\n        \"Conservation Status\": \"Fragile habitats under threat from a range of human activities and environmental stressors\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ocean floor\",\n      \"type\": \"Geographical Feature\",\n      \"description\": \"The ocean floor is the bottom surface of the ocean, which includes various features such as plains, mountains, and coral reefs. It plays a crucial role in marine ecosystems and ocean dynamics.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Coverage by Coral Reefs\": \"Less than 1%\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"coastal protection\",\n      \"type\": \"Ecosystem Service\",\n      \"description\": \"Coastal protection is a critical ecosystem service provided by coral reefs, which act as natural barriers to mitigate the destructive effects of natural disasters such as hurricanes and tsunamis.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Importance\": \"Critical\",\n        \"Benefit\": \"Mitigates destructive effects of natural disasters\",\n        \"Type of Natural Disasters\": \"Hurricanes and tsunamis\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"coastal communities\",\n      \"type\": \"Human Settlement\",\n      \"description\": \"Coastal communities are human settlements located near the coast, which benefit from the protective and ecological services provided by coral reefs.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Location\": \"Near the coast\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"coastal areas\",\n      \"type\": \"Geographical Location\",\n      \"description\": \"Coastal areas are regions where the land meets the sea, often characterized by unique ecosystems and significant human activity. These areas are crucial for tourism, fisheries, and environmental health, but they are also vulnerable to various threats including climate change, pollution, and unsustainable practices.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Ecosystem Importance\": \"High, due to the presence of coral reefs and other fragile habitats\",\n        \"Human Activity\": \"Significant, including tourism, fishing, and pollution\",\n        \"Vulnerability\": \"High, threatened by climate change, pollution, and unsustainable management practices\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Overfishing\",\n      \"type\": \"Environmental Issue\",\n      \"description\": \"Overfishing is the removal of a species of fish from a body of water at a rate faster than the species can replenish itself, leading to a decline in the population of that species.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Impact\": \"Contributes to the decline of coral reefs\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Destructive fishing practices\",\n      \"type\": \"Activity\",\n      \"description\": \"Destructive fishing practices are methods of fishing that cause significant damage to the marine environment, particularly to coral reefs, and contribute to the decline of these ecosystems.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Impact\": \"Contributes to the decline of coral reefs\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Algae\",\n      \"type\": \"Organism\",\n      \"description\": \"Algae are photosynthetic organisms that live in the tissues of corals, providing them with essential nutrients through a symbiotic relationship.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Role\": \"Photosynthetic Organism\",\n        \"Habitat\": \"Coral Tissues\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Environmental Stressors\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Environmental stressors are factors that can cause harm or disruption to ecosystems, often leading to degradation or loss of habitat. They can be both natural and human-induced, and they pose significant threats to fragile habitats, particularly coral reefs.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Impact\": \"Harmful to fragile habitats and marine ecosystems\",\n        \"Origin\": \"Both natural and human-induced\",\n        \"Examples\": \"Pollution from land-based sources, agricultural runoff, plastic waste\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Marine Life\",\n      \"type\": \"Biological Community\",\n      \"description\": \"A wide variety of marine organisms, including fish, invertebrates, and plants, that rely on coral reefs for food, shelter, and breeding grounds\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Fisheries\",\n      \"type\": \"Industry\",\n      \"description\": \"Local and global fishing industries that provide food and income for millions of people\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n